\section{Discussion and Conclusion}
\label{sec:discussion}

\paragraph{Boundary conditions and mechanisms.}
The two-dimensional decomposition applies to cross-domain schemas; same-domain schemas exhibit centrality confounding (\S\ref{sec:centrality_confound}). Separability is confirmed on FewRel and DocRED (\S\ref{sec:multi_channel}); logit-scale evidence is inconclusive. The RE effect replicates across four models from three families (8B--70B; Gemini Flash), two formats, five prompts, and two RE datasets; the NER null is confirmed on two models. SCS captures semantic proximity in LLMs' type-resolution space: individually weak pairwise signals ($R^2 = 1.3\%$) compound into operationally significant batch effects ($R^2 = 22\text{--}58\%$; Appendix~\ref{app:aggregation-sim})---a pattern invisible to per-type evaluation and not previously quantified in the IE literature. The NER--RE asymmetry reveals structurally different error modes: RE errors arise from type-label confusion in the output space, while NER errors stem from span-boundary decisions largely independent of label similarity \citep{tam-2024-let-me-speak,schall-2025-hidden-cost}---with direct implications for task-specific mitigation. Partial correlation confirms the BCS signal after controlling for degree centrality (Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_partial_corr}).

\paragraph{Practical implications and conclusion.}
\label{sec:conclusion}
For NER, reducing candidate types per prompt is the primary lever. For RE, practitioners can compute BCS as a pre-hoc diagnostic before deployment: schemas exceeding an empirical threshold (e.g., SCS${}\,>\,0.85$ for type pairs) flag potential accuracy degradation without any extraction runs. The 22--58\% explained variance means BCS monitoring can anticipate roughly half of cross-schema performance variation at zero annotation cost. The SDGD failure establishes that na\"{i}ve decompose-then-merge is not viable; however, oracle routing recovers substantial accuracy (72.4\% vs.\ 50.4\%; Appendix~\ref{sec:appendix_routing}), suggesting routing-aware decomposition as a concrete path for future work. In sum, training-free LLM extraction degrades along two separable dimensions---count-associated recall decline and confusability-associated type substitution---replicated across four models for RE, with NER null confirmed on two models.

